                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Challenge",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ": There are three self-producing integers with 10 digits. This is probably a job for a computer program if you feel like having a bash at it.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6333176664$, $9753086421$ and $9975084201$.",
          "worked": "A program can enumerate the digit multisets of length ten. For each multiset, form the descending and ascending numbers, subtract, and retain the result if repeating the operation leaves it unchanged. Remove duplicate results and exclude zero.\n\nThe three results check as follows:\n$$\\begin{align*}7766664331-1334666677&=6333176664\\\\9876543210-0123456789&=9753086421\\\\9987542100-0012457899&=9975084201.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
